no matter who you are  learning about poetry is a huge source  of power you too can write words that  will set the world on fire  we've braved the belly of the beast  we've learned that quiet isn't always  peace  and the norms and notions of what just  is  isn't always  just this  [Music]  you're going to learn not only how to be  a great poet but how to be a change  maker  when i was first writing poems what made  them so  special to me was that experience of  having my feelings  articulated and named on the page i  could verbalize what was going on in  here that people didn't know for there  was always light if only we're brave  enough to see it if only we're brave  enough  to be it  you should write at least once every day  you can write gibberish you can draw  scarecrows like you can do whatever just  get your pen moving i'm going to be  sharing ugly drafts of my own poems and  show you what it means to perform in  front of an audience trying to be heard  but these words don't sound right could  i ever be  in the spotlight  when i was little i had a speech  impediment which made it very difficult  for me to speak up for myself a lot of  my first few poems were about what it  was like to be lonely because i might  not look or speak like the students  around me  there's always another story to write  always another verse waiting on the  horizon we all can harness the power of  poetry to become stronger communicators  better leaders and also more  compassionate people  i'm amanda gorman and this is  masterclass  [Music]  i want to be the teacher i never had  [Music]  you
 

